together so the color and sheen line up."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why do gaps show up between boards in the winter?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Forced-air and baseboard heat dry the air out, and wood gives up moisture and shrinks. Small seasonal gaps in January that close up by summer are normal for solid strip floors. Running a humidifier to keep indoor humidity in the range the manufacturer recommends keeps them smaller."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How long does a hardwood installation take?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A typical bedroom in prefinished engineered flooring is often one to two days on site after acclimation. A site-finished first floor with sanding, stain and several coats usually runs about a week, because each coat needs time to dry before the next one goes on."}}]}</script><!-- First-touch attribution. Runs before anything else so a click-id is never
